{
  "title": "Conway's Game of Life",
  "slug": "conways-game-of-life",
  "hue": 150,
  "lede": "A grid of cells that live, die or are born by four simple rules. John Conway devised it in 1970, and it can compute anything a computer can.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Paint cells, press play",
      "body": "<style>\n.gl{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;gap:16px;grid-template-columns:1fr;font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg)}\n.gl *{box-sizing:border-box}\n@media (min-width:820px){.gl{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 264px;gap:24px;align-items:start}}\n.gl-q{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;font-weight:600}\n.gl-q b{color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.gl-board{position:relative;border-radius:16px;background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);padding:10px}\n.gl-cv{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;touch-action:none;cursor:crosshair;border-radius:8px}\n.gl-cv:focus-visible{outline:3px solid color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) 55%,transparent);outline-offset:3px}\n.gl-stats{display:flex;gap:18px;margin:8px 2px 0;font-size:14px;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.gl-stats b{font-family:var(--ow-mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ow-fg);font-weight:600;margin-left:6px}\n.gl-side{display:grid;gap:12px}\n.gl-box{padding:14px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-panel)}\n.gl-row{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center}\n.gl-play{appearance:none;flex:none;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;border:0;background:var(--ow-accent);color:var(--ow-accent-ink);cursor:pointer;display:grid;place-items:center;touch-action:manipulation}\n.gl-play svg{width:18px;height:18px;display:block}\n.gl-btn{appearance:none;font:inherit;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;min-height:40px;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:999px;border:1.5px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-bg);color:var(--ow-fg);cursor:pointer;touch-action:manipulation}\n.gl-btn:hover,.gl-chip:hover{border-color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.gl button:focus-visible,.gl input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) 55%,transparent);outline-offset:2px}\n.gl-lab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-top:12px}\n.gl-lab output{font-family:var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-muted);font-weight:500}\n.gl input[type=range]{width:100%;margin:6px 0 0;height:28px;accent-color:var(--ow-accent);cursor:pointer}\n.gl-h{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.gl-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n.gl-chip{appearance:none;font:inherit;font-size:14px;min-height:40px;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:999px;border:1.5px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-bg);color:var(--ow-fg);cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;touch-action:manipulation}\n.gl-chip svg{width:16px;height:16px;flex:none}\n.gl-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--ow-fg);border-color:var(--ow-fg);color:var(--ow-bg)}\n.gl-rules{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;display:grid;gap:5px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.gl-rules b{color:var(--ow-fg);font-weight:650}\n.gl-say{margin:8px 2px 0;font-size:14px;color:var(--ow-muted);min-height:1.4em}\n@media (max-width:819px){.gl-side{grid-template-columns:1fr}.gl-rbox{display:none}}\n@media (min-width:520px) and (max-width:819px){.gl-side{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"gl\">\n  <div>\n    <p class=\"gl-q\"><b>Paint</b> live cells with your mouse or finger, then press <b>play</b>.</p>\n    <div class=\"gl-board\">\n      <canvas class=\"gl-cv\" id=\"gl-cv\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Game of Life grid, 40 by 24 cells. Arrow keys move the cursor, Space or Enter toggles a cell.\"></canvas>\n      <div class=\"gl-stats\" aria-live=\"off\"><span>Generation<b id=\"gl-gen\">0</b></span><span>Population<b id=\"gl-pop\">0</b></span></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"gl-say\" id=\"gl-say\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"gl-side\">\n    <div class=\"gl-box\">\n      <div class=\"gl-row\">\n        <button class=\"gl-play\" type=\"button\" id=\"gl-go\" aria-label=\"Play\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path id=\"gl-ic\" d=\"M5 3l12 7-12 7z\"/></svg></button>\n        <button class=\"gl-btn\" type=\"button\" id=\"gl-step\">Step</button>\n        <button class=\"gl-btn\" type=\"button\" id=\"gl-clr\">Clear</button>\n      </div>\n      <label class=\"gl-lab\" for=\"gl-sp\"><span>Speed</span><output id=\"gl-spo\" for=\"gl-sp\">8 gen/s</output></label>\n      <input id=\"gl-sp\" type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"30\" step=\"1\" value=\"8\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"gl-box\">\n      <p class=\"gl-h\">One tap patterns</p>\n      <div class=\"gl-chips\" id=\"gl-pre\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"gl-box gl-rbox\">\n      <p class=\"gl-h\">The four rules</p>\n      <ul class=\"gl-rules\">\n        <li><b>Under 2</b> live neighbours: dies</li>\n        <li><b>2 or 3</b>: lives on</li>\n        <li><b>Over 3</b>: dies</li>\n        <li><b>Exactly 3</b> around an empty cell: born</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var W=40,H=24,M=12,GW=W+2*M,GH=H+2*M;\n  var g=new Uint8Array(GW*GH),fade=new Float32Array(W*H),gen=0;\n  var cv=document.getElementById('gl-cv'),ctx=cv.getContext('2d');\n  var genEl=document.getElementById('gl-gen'),popEl=document.getElementById('gl-pop'),say=document.getElementById('gl-say');\n  var reduce=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;\n  var P={\n    glider:{name:'Glider',note:'A glider: it walks one cell diagonally every 4 generations.',rows:['.O.','..O','OOO'],at:[3,3]},\n    gun:{name:'Glider gun',note:'Gosper’s glider gun fires a new glider every 30 generations, forever.',rows:['........................O...........','......................O.O...........','............OO......OO............OO','...........O...O....OO............OO','OO........O.....O...OO..............','OO........O...O.OO....O.O...........','..........O.....O.......O...........','...........O...O....................','............OO......................'],at:[2,1]},\n    pulsar:{name:'Pulsar',note:'A pulsar: an oscillator that repeats every 3 generations.',rows:['..OOO...OOO..','.............','O....O.O....O','O....O.O....O','O....O.O....O','..OOO...OOO..','.............','..OOO...OOO..','O....O.O....O','O....O.O....O','O....O.O....O','.............','..OOO...OOO..'],at:[13,5]},\n    random:{name:'Random',note:'A random soup: watch it settle into still lifes and blinkers.'}\n  };\n  var icons={glider:'M7 1h3v3H7zM10 6h3v3h-3zM3 11h3v3H3zM7 11h3v3H7zM11 11h3v3h-3z',gun:'M1 6h4v4H1zM6 4h2v8H6zM9 3h2v10H9zM12 6h3v4h-3z',pulsar:'M2 2h3v3H2zM11 2h3v3h-3zM2 11h3v3H2zM11 11h3v3h-3zM6.5 6.5h3v3h-3z',random:'M2 3h3v3H2zM9 2h3v3H9zM5 8h3v3H5zM11 10h3v3h-3zM2 12h3v3H2z'};\n  var pre=document.getElementById('gl-pre'),chips={};\n  Object.keys(P).forEach(function(k){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='gl-chip';b.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false');\n    b.innerHTML='<svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"'+icons[k]+'\"/></svg>'+P[k].name;\n    b.addEventListener('click',function(){load(k)});pre.appendChild(b);chips[k]=b;\n  });\n  function idx(x,y){return (y+M)*GW+x+M}\n  function clear(){g=new Uint8Array(GW*GH);fade=new Float32Array(W*H);gen=0}\n  var seed=7;function rnd(){seed=(seed*16807)%2147483647;return seed/2147483647}\n  function load(k){\n    stop();clear();\n    if(k==='random'){for(var y=0;y<H;y++)for(var x=0;x<W;x++)if(rnd()<.3)g[idx(x,y)]=1}\n    else P[k].rows.forEach(function(r,y){for(var x=0;x<r.length;x++)if(r[x]==='O')g[idx(x+P[k].at[0],y+P[k].at[1])]=1});\n    Object.keys(chips).forEach(function(c){chips[c].setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(c===k))});\n    say.textContent=P[k].note;draw();\n  }\n  function step(){\n    var n=new Uint8Array(GW*GH);\n    for(var y=1;y<GH-1;y++){var r=y*GW;for(var x=1;x<GW-1;x++){var i=r+x,c=g[i-GW-1]+g[i-GW]+g[i-GW+1]+g[i-1]+g[i+1]+g[i+GW-1]+g[i+GW]+g[i+GW+1];n[i]=(c===3||(c===2&&g[i]))?1:0}}\n    for(var yy=0;yy<H;yy++)for(var xx=0;xx<W;xx++){var j=yy*W+xx;if(g[idx(xx,yy)]&&!n[idx(xx,yy)])fade[j]=1;else fade[j]*=.6}\n    g=n;gen++;\n  }\n  var cell=12,pad=0,colors={};\n  function readColors(){var s=getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);['--ow-accent','--ow-line','--ow-fg','--ow-panel','--ow-muted'].forEach(function(k){colors[k]=s.getPropertyValue(k).trim()||'#888'})}\n  function size(){\n    var w=cv.parentElement.clientWidth-20;cell=Math.max(6,Math.floor(w/W));\n    var dpr=window.devicePixelRatio||1;cv.width=cell*W*dpr;cv.height=cell*H*dpr;cv.style.width=cell*W+'px';cv.style.height=cell*H+'px';\n    ctx.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0);draw();\n  }\n  var cur={x:20,y:12,show:false};\n  function draw(){\n    ctx.clearRect(0,0,cell*W,cell*H);\n    ctx.fillStyle=colors['--ow-line'];ctx.globalAlpha=.55;\n    for(var x=1;x<W;x++)ctx.fillRect(x*cell,0,1,cell*H);\n    for(var y=1;y<H;y++)ctx.fillRect(0,y*cell,cell*W,1);\n    var pop=0,gap=cell>9?1.5:1,rad=Math.max(1,cell*.22);\n    for(y=0;y<H;y++)for(x=0;x<W;x++){\n      var on=g[idx(x,y)],f=fade[y*W+x];\n      if(on){pop++;ctx.globalAlpha=1;ctx.fillStyle=colors['--ow-accent']}\n      else if(f>.05){ctx.globalAlpha=f*.28;ctx.fillStyle=colors['--ow-accent']}\n      else continue;\n      ctx.beginPath();if(ctx.roundRect)ctx.roundRect(x*cell+gap,y*cell+gap,cell-2*gap,cell-2*gap,rad);else ctx.rect(x*cell+gap,y*cell+gap,cell-2*gap,cell-2*gap);ctx.fill();\n    }\n    if(cur.show){ctx.globalAlpha=1;ctx.strokeStyle=colors['--ow-fg'];ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.strokeRect(cur.x*cell+1,cur.y*cell+1,cell-2,cell-2)}\n    ctx.globalAlpha=1;\n    genEl.textContent=gen;popEl.textContent=pop;\n    if(running===false&&pop===0&&gen>0)say.textContent='Everything died. Paint again or pick a pattern.';\n  }\n  var running=false,raf=0,last=0,acc=0,sp=document.getElementById('gl-sp'),spo=document.getElementById('gl-spo');\n  var go=document.getElementById('gl-go'),ic=document.getElementById('gl-ic');\n  function speed(){return +sp.value}\n  sp.addEventListener('input',function(){spo.textContent=sp.value+' gen/s';sp.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',sp.value+' generations per second')});\n  function loop(ts){\n    if(!running)return;\n    if(!last)last=ts;acc+=(ts-last)/1000;last=ts;\n    var dt=1/speed(),k=0;while(acc>=dt&&k<4){step();acc-=dt;k++}\n    if(k>=4)acc=0;\n    if(k)draw();\n    raf=requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n  }\n  function start(){if(running)return;running=true;last=0;acc=1/speed();ic.setAttribute('d','M5 3h3.5v14H5zM11.5 3H15v14h-3.5z');go.setAttribute('aria-label','Pause');raf=requestAnimationFrame(loop)}\n  function stop(){running=false;if(raf)cancelAnimationFrame(raf);raf=0;ic.setAttribute('d','M5 3l12 7-12 7z');go.setAttribute('aria-label','Play')}\n  go.addEventListener('click',function(){running?stop():start()});\n  document.getElementById('gl-step').addEventListener('click',function(){stop();step();draw()});\n  document.getElementById('gl-clr').addEventListener('click',function(){stop();clear();Object.keys(chips).forEach(function(c){chips[c].setAttribute('aria-pressed','false')});say.textContent='Empty grid. Paint a few cells: three in a row make a blinker.';draw()});\n  function unpress(){Object.keys(chips).forEach(function(c){chips[c].setAttribute('aria-pressed','false')})}\n  var painting=false,paintVal=1;\n  function cellAt(e){var b=cv.getBoundingClientRect();return{x:Math.floor((e.clientX-b.left)/b.width*W),y:Math.floor((e.clientY-b.top)/b.height*H)}}\n  function paint(c){if(c.x<0||c.y<0||c.x>=W||c.y>=H)return;g[idx(c.x,c.y)]=paintVal;draw()}\n  cv.addEventListener('pointerdown',function(e){e.preventDefault();cv.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);var c=cellAt(e);if(c.x<0||c.y<0||c.x>=W||c.y>=H)return;painting=true;paintVal=g[idx(c.x,c.y)]?0:1;unpress();paint(c)});\n  cv.addEventListener('pointermove',function(e){if(painting)paint(cellAt(e))});\n  cv.addEventListener('pointerup',function(){painting=false});\n  cv.addEventListener('pointercancel',function(){painting=false});\n  cv.addEventListener('focus',function(){cur.show=true;draw()});\n  cv.addEventListener('blur',function(){cur.show=false;draw()});\n  cv.addEventListener('keydown',function(e){\n    var d={ArrowLeft:[-1,0],ArrowRight:[1,0],ArrowUp:[0,-1],ArrowDown:[0,1]}[e.key];\n    if(d){e.preventDefault();cur.x=Math.max(0,Math.min(W-1,cur.x+d[0]));cur.y=Math.max(0,Math.min(H-1,cur.y+d[1]));draw()}\n    else if(e.key===' '||e.key==='Enter'){e.preventDefault();var i=idx(cur.x,cur.y);g[i]=g[i]?0:1;unpress();draw()}\n  });\n  if(reduce){sp.value=3;spo.textContent='3 gen/s'}\n  readColors();load('gun');\n  say.textContent='Gosper’s glider gun is loaded. Press play, or tap another pattern.';\n  size();\n  var rt=0;window.addEventListener('resize',function(){clearTimeout(rt);rt=setTimeout(size,80)});\n})();\n</script>\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Four rules, zero players",
      "body": "Life is a zero-player game: its evolution is determined by its initial state, requiring no further input [1]. Each cell counts its eight neighbours. A live cell with two or three live neighbours survives, a dead cell with exactly three is born, and every other cell dies or stays empty [2][3]. Conway chose the rules after a long period of experimentation [4], so that the behaviour of a population would be unpredictable [5].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "meaning that its evolution is determined by its initial state, requiring no further input"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Any live cell with two or three live neighbours lives on to the next generation."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Any dead cell with exactly three live neighbours becomes a live cell, as if by reproduction."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/lifepatterns/october1970.html",
          "title": "Martin Gardner, \"The fantastic combinations of John Conway's new solitaire game 'life'\", Scientific American, October 1970 (transcription)",
          "quote": "Conway chose his rules carefully, after a long period of experimentation"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/lifepatterns/october1970.html",
          "title": "Martin Gardner, \"The fantastic combinations of John Conway's new solitaire game 'life'\", Scientific American, October 1970 (transcription)",
          "quote": "the rules should be such as to make the behavior of the population unpredictable"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Gliders, guns and Turing completeness",
      "body": "Patterns fall into still lifes, which never change; oscillators, which return to their start after a fixed number of generations; and spaceships, which travel across the grid [1]. The glider rebuilds itself every four generations one cell further along a diagonal [2]. Conway offered $50 for a proof either way that no pattern grows without limit [3]. An MIT team led by Bill Gosper won it in November 1970 [4] with a gun that fires a new glider every 30 generations [5]. Life is as powerful as any computer with unlimited memory: it is Turing complete [6].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Common pattern types include still lifes, which do not change from one generation to the next; oscillators, which return to their initial state after a finite number of generations; and spaceships, which translate themselves across the grid."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/lifepatterns/october1970.html",
          "title": "Martin Gardner, \"The fantastic combinations of John Conway's new solitaire game 'life'\", Scientific American, October 1970 (transcription)",
          "quote": "the glider replicates itself in the same orientation after four moves, and has traveled one cell diagonally"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/lifepatterns/october1970.html",
          "title": "Martin Gardner, \"The fantastic combinations of John Conway's new solitaire game 'life'\", Scientific American, October 1970 (transcription)",
          "quote": "Conway has offered a prize of $50 to the first person who can prove or disprove the conjecture"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The prize was won in November by a team from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, led by Bill Gosper"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "produces its first glider on the 15th generation, and another glider every 30th generation from then on"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "so the Game of Life is theoretically as powerful as any computer with unlimited memory and no time constraints; it is Turing complete"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "What Conway thought of it",
      "body": "Life first appeared in the October 1970 Scientific American [1], in Martin Gardner's column, which was based on personal conversations with Conway [2]. It became the most widely read of all Gardner's columns and made Conway an instant celebrity [3]. Conway later came to dislike how talk about him centred on Life, feeling it overshadowed deeper and more important work, though he stayed proud of it [4]. The game helped launch a new branch of mathematics, cellular automata [5].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The game made its first public appearance in the October 1970 issue of Scientific American"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conway%27s_Game_of_Life",
          "title": "Conway's Game of Life (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "column, which was based on personal conversations with Conway"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Horton_Conway",
          "title": "John Horton Conway (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "it became the most widely read of all his columns and made Conway an instant celebrity"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Horton_Conway",
          "title": "John Horton Conway (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Conway came to dislike how discussions of him heavily focused on his Game of Life, feeling that it overshadowed deeper and more important things he had done, although he remained proud of his work on it."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Horton_Conway",
          "title": "John Horton Conway (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The game helped to launch a new branch of mathematics, the field of cellular automata."
        }
